# clause-ir — Design

Leaf-dep crate carrying data contracts shared across every compiler
phase. No algorithmic content.

## Scope

Types consumed by two or more phase crates:

- `Span` — source span: `{ file: FileId, start: ByteOffset, end: ByteOffset }`.
  Carries original positions for diagnostics and incremental-build
  invalidation.
- `FileId` — dense interned identifier for a loaded source file.
  Plan-time assigned by the workspace driver.
- `NodeId` — dense interned identifier for AST nodes. Assigned at
  parse time; stable across later phases for cross-phase
  annotations (resolution info, type info).
- `ScopeId` — dense interned identifier for lexical scopes.
- `Diagnostic` — `{ severity, span, message, labels }`. The common
  error / warning / info structure.
- `Severity` — enum: `Error`, `Warning`, `Info`, `Help`.
- `TokenKind` — enum discriminating lex tokens. Shared between
  `clause-lex` (producer) and `clause-syntax` (consumer).
- `AstNodeKind` — enum discriminating AST nodes. Shared between
  `clause-syntax` (producer) and downstream phases.

## Non-scope

- Parsers, resolvers, typecheckers — each phase owns its own
  algorithms.
- Token + AST concrete representations (the node types themselves)
  live in their producing crate; `clause-ir` only hosts the
  discriminator enums and the common annotation slots.
- Rendering of diagnostics (color, unicode art) — that's the
  `clause` binary's renderer.

## Dependencies

- arvo (for `USize`, `Cap`, newtype discipline).
- No other hilavitkutin or clause deps.
- `#![no_std]`, no alloc.

## Provisional module layout

- `span.rs` — Span, FileId, ByteOffset.
- `ids.rs` — NodeId, ScopeId + dense-interning helpers.
- `diagnostic.rs` — Diagnostic, Severity, Label.
- `tokens.rs` — TokenKind.
- `nodes.rs` — AstNodeKind + shared node annotation slots.

